  "body": "**Audit / independent check; no \u03ba claim.** This PR certifies the exact pattern-integer optimum of the whole-helper owner fill for the two latest T74 claims, and compares each published fill with it.\n\n| claim | published fill idle | exact pattern optimum (unique within 1e-12) | gap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [#2374](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2374) on #2322's words, \u03ba = 0.0016971949509 | `{1:21978, 3:8592, 5:2552, 32:1, 48:24560}` | **the same** | 0 (every fill has b \u2264 \u03ba + 1e-15) |\n| [#2435](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2435) on its copy-buffer-raised words, \u03ba = 0.0016985113437 | `{1:20824, 3:6695, 5:1, 48:25302}` | **`{1:20822, 3:6694, 5:2, 48:25302}`**, root 0.0016985119240 | **+5.80e-10 available** |\n\n- **#2374:** its claim of \"an exact window-free-optimal owner fill\" is confirmed and strengthened to optimality over *all* legal whole-helper fills. Owner-map work on #2322's words is exactly exhausted; #2402's cap allowed up to 8.1e-10.\n- **#2435:** its \"exact owner fill for the new inventory\" is not the pattern optimum. The optimum moves two rank-1 remainders and one rank-3 remainder into one more rank-5 remainder. It uses, for example, two (32: 9,9,9) bins and 1,156 (48: 4,8,9,9,9,9) bins. The full pattern counts are in the receipt, as a concrete owner-level target worth up to +5.8e-10. Whether it can be realized under #2435's windows and families is **not** checked here.\n\n**Method** (`owner_optimum.py`, standard library only, about 45 s).\n- **Relaxation.** Every legal fill places each helper role whole in one idle bin of rank 8, 16, 32 or 48. That is an integer pattern-count vector over the 1,163 width patterns with fixed bin and inventory row sums, so it relaxes every legal fill. This is the #2387 / #2360 relaxation, after #1129.\n- **Steps, per claim:**\n  1. Certify the published idle multiset's root within \u00b11e-15 of the claimed \u03ba, using 800-bit enclosures.\n  2. Enumerate exactly, by budget-pruned DFS with exact rational basis solves, every integer solution that could beat the claim. Degenerate zero-remainder swaps are handled with an integrality and nonnegativity argument.\n  3. Certify the best solution's root.\n  4. At (best root) + 1e-15, an exact rational dual, feasible against lower enclosures on all patterns, leaves **zero** integer survivors.\n  5. Control at (best root) \u2212 1e-12: the optimum survives, and every survivor has its idle multiset.\n- **Inputs.**\n  - The #2322 profile and inventory were recounted in #2402.\n  - #2435's two words, at head `324d7d35`, were recounted with the #2387 frame-climb rule. They match its reported profile {1:2359, 2:632, 3:330, 4:120, 5:38, 8:8} and inventory {4:33, 5:9, 7:62, 8:90, 9:240}.\n  - Idle multisets and \u03ba are as published.\n- **Review.** An adversarial AI reviewer could not refute the #2374 part. It reproduced the root to 60 digits and ran a Gomory group-relaxation check, which found the only correction within budget is one empty 32-bin. It also ran more than 48,000 local exchange moves with no improvement; its best alternative is 5.0e-10 below. Its two wording issues are fixed. The #2435 extension uses the same code path.\n- **Checks.** `--check-only`, the 3.10 grammar check and the research tests pass. Run on CPython 3.14.4; the registered 3.12 replay was not run.\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/t74-owner-fill-optimality/owner_optimum.py\n# PASS_T74_OWNER_OPTIMUM pr2374:claim_is_optimum pr2435:optimum_gain=+5.803e-10 unique_within_1e-12 no_new_kappa\n```\n\n**Scope.** The pattern relaxation drops windows, families and ports, so the upper bounds cover every legal fill. Realization of any fill is not re-run, neither the claimants' fills nor #2435's optimum. Base: main `0fdd7d82`. Card: `independent-moment`, scope refined; the assignment is the adversarial-audit track, seed 71.\n\n**Credits.**\n- #2374 / #2435 / #2349 (Jeremy Kothe) and #2363 (mason-hale): the audited fills.\n- #2322 (Vlado Vojdanovski): the words.\n- #2360 (Jeremy Diviney) and #1129 (Ali Romman): the pattern-dual relaxation.\n- #2387 / #2402 (this author): the tools, vendored with pins.\n\nPrepared with substantial AI assistance (Claude Code, Anthropic, Claude Opus 5.5). No independent human review is claimed. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
